# GalixiHub Docker Deployment with Docker Compose

This repository contains the Docker deployment infrastructure for 
running a GalixiHub server.

It provides Docker Compose configuration, startup scripts, and 
environment configuration used to launch a GalixiHub containerized 
instance.

This repository DOES NOT contain the GalixiHub software itself.

The GalixiHub server is distributed as a Docker image.

---
## Repository Contents

internal/docker-compose.yml
Defines the GalixiHub and MariaDB containers.

internal/init-galixihub.sql
Configures the GalixiHub MariaDB database

galixihub.env
Configuration file for initial setup. This MUST be modified by the 
user before starting the GalixiHub application.

galixistart.sh
Starts the GalixiHub Docker stack.

galixistop.sh
Stops the GalixiHub Docker stack.

---
## Requirements

The following software must be installed:

```
Docker
Docker Compose (Docker CLI plugin)
```

The host system must also allow network access to the ports defined in 
the configuration file (galixihub.env).

---
## Installation

Enter the directory:
cd galixihub-compose

Edit the configuration file:
nano galixihub.env

Adjust values as required for your server.
Note: Before starting GalixiHub, the GALIXIHUB_ACCEPT_LICENSE must be
set to YES (GALIXIHUB_ACCEPT_LICENSE=YES). This accepts the propietary
license used in the GalixiHub Docker image. 

---
## Starting GalixiHub

Run the startup script:
sudo ./galixistart.sh

The script will:
* Load configuration values
* Start Docker containers
* Wait for MariaDB readiness
* Launch the GalixiHub server

## Stopping GalixiHub

To stop the running stack:
sudo ./galixistop.sh

To REMOVE the full container, including database information:
sudo ./galixistop.sh -r

---
## Configuration

Initial configuration is defined in:
galixihub.env


Important variables include:
GALIXIHUB_WORLD_NAME
GALIXIHUB_HOSTNAME
GALIXIHUB_PORT
GALIXIHUB_OWNER_CODE

These values are used during initial world creation.

After a world has been created some values cannot be changed.

